@h1 Structure & layout h1@

Headings give a document its outline; sectioning wrappers give it a skeleton;
lists, quotes, and rules set pieces apart; rows and columns place blocks side by
side. Every one is a node — no CSS, no floats.

@h2 Headings h2@

Six levels, @@@code @h1 code@@@ through @@@code @h6 code@@@. Level one is the
title; deeper levels nest under it to trace your argument.

@@@pre
@h1 Coastal survey 2024 h1@
@h2 Methods h2@
@h3 Tide-gauge calibration h3@
pre@@@

Each renders straight into its tag — @@@code <h1>Coastal survey 2024</h1> code@@@ —
with no paragraph around the text. Don't skip a level for a smaller heading; the
jump breaks the outline, and size is a
@a |href /docs/write/rendering/| rendering a@ concern.

@h2 Sectioning wrappers h2@

Semantic containers describe the shape of the page. Each maps to the same-named
HTML element that a screen reader, print engine, or search index looks for:

@@@pre
@article … article@   a self-contained piece
@section … section@   a thematic division
@header  … header@    an opening block (title, byline)
@footer  … footer@    a closing block (date, credits)
@nav     … nav@        navigation links
@aside   … aside@      supporting or marginal content
@main    … main@       the primary content region
pre@@@

Nest them and the document gains real structure:

@@@pre
@article
@header
@h1 A survey of the northern reef h1@
header@

@section
The season opened early this year.
section@

@footer
@small Published 2024. small@
footer@
article@
pre@@@

That builds an @@@code <article> code@@@ holding a @@@code <header> code@@@,
@@@code <section> code@@@, and @@@code <footer> code@@@. A @@@code @section code@@@
already paragraph-wraps its prose, so don't add an inner @@@code @p … p@ code@@@.

@h2 Generic containers h2@

When you need a box to style or label and no semantic wrapper fits, use the
block @@@code @div code@@@ or inline @@@code @span code@@@. Both accept
@code |class …| code@ and @code |id …| code@ to hook them for CSS:

@@@pre
@div |class callout-card|
A boxed note, grouped for styling.
div@

An @span |id lede| opening clause span@ inside a sentence.
pre@@@

The block becomes a @@@code <div> code@@@, the inline one a
@@@code <span> code@@@. @a |href /docs/write/rendering/| Rendering a@ covers how a
class name reaches your stylesheet.

@h2 Bulleted & numbered lists h2@

A list is a list node holding one @@@code @li code@@@ per item. The theme draws
the markers — never type a dash or a number yourself.

@@@pre
@ul
@li Salt marsh li@
@li Mud flat li@
@li Shingle bank li@
ul@
pre@@@

Swap @@@code @ul code@@@ for @@@code @ol code@@@ and the numbers come
automatically; reorder items and they renumber for free:

@@@pre
@ol
@li Record the water level. li@
@li Note wind direction. li@
@li Photograph the transect. li@
ol@
pre@@@

@h2 Definition lists h2@

A @@@code @dl code@@@ pairs a term (@@@code @dt code@@@) with its description
(@@@code @dd code@@@) — a glossary, a field key, a set of parameters:

@@@pre
@dl
@dt Transect dt@
@dd A fixed line along which measurements are repeated. dd@
@dt Datum dt@
@dd The reference level all heights are measured from. dd@
dl@
pre@@@

@h2 Items hold rich content h2@

An item is inline-context: a one-line item flattens to just its text, with no
inner paragraph. But it can still carry marks, links, or a nested list — drop a
whole list node inside an item's body to nest:

@@@pre
@ul
@li The _daily_ readings, taken at dawn. li@
@li Supplies aboard the tender:
@ul
@li spare batteries li@
@li calibration weights li@
ul@
li@
ul@
pre@@@

@h2 Block quotations h2@

A @@@code @blockquote code@@@ lifts a passage off the page — an epigraph, a
pulled quote, a cited paragraph. The theme adds a left rule and muted colour:

@@@pre
@blockquote
"The sea, once it casts its spell, holds one in its net of wonder forever."
— Jacques Cousteau
blockquote@
pre@@@

For a short quoted phrase inside a sentence, plain quotation marks are enough.

@h2 Preformatted text h2@

A @@@code @pre code@@@ block renders monospaced — a code sample, a data
fragment, anything shown in a fixed-width face:

@@@pre
@pre gauge.read() -> 2.41 m pre@
pre@@@

@aside(class note) 💡 An honest limit: @@@code @pre code@@@ renders monospaced,
but its body still passes through normal paragraph-wrapping, so it is not a
strict significant-whitespace block. Where exact indentation and line breaks
_must_ survive, build the file and check the output. aside@

@h2 Horizontal rule h2@

A self-closing divider — a visual break with no heading. It takes no body:

@@@pre
The first movement ends here.

@hr

The second begins.
pre@@@

That produces a plain @@@code <hr> code@@@.

@h2 Side-by-side: rows & columns h2@

A @@@code @row code@@@ is an invisible flexbox that lays its columns out
horizontally. A @@@code @col |size 260| code@@@ fixes a column's width; a bare
@@@code @col code@@@ fills whatever space is left. Put anything in a column —
prose, an image, a table:

@@@pre
@row
@col |size 260|
@img |src ./gauge.png| |alt The tide gauge|
col@
@col
The gauge logged every hour of every tide, its readings the backbone of the
season's survey.
col@
row@
pre@@@

The fixed-plus-flexible pair is the workhorse for an image beside its
explanation. Two bare columns split the row evenly — here it is live:

@row
@col
_The lamp room._ Glass on every side and a lens that threw the beam twenty miles
out to the shipping lanes.
col@
@col
_The watch room._ Below the light, a desk, a barometer, and the log where every
hour of every night was accounted for.
col@
row@

A size takes a named preset (small, medium, large — 220, 380, 600 pixels), a
pixel number, or a percentage; several bare columns share the leftover equally.
The row wraps: when the viewport or printed page is too narrow, the columns stack
— two columns on a wide screen, one readable column on a phone, no media query.
Separate a row from surrounding prose with blank lines so it stays top-level.

@h2 See also h2@

@ul
@li @a |href /docs/write/prose/| Writing prose a@ — text, emphasis, and the inline marks these blocks hold. li@
@li @a |href /docs/write/tables/| Tables a@ — a captioned table to place inside a column. li@
@li @a |href /docs/write/media/| Images & media a@ — sizing a figure in a fixed column. li@
ul@
